eived_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Pre-registration: matched-progress confirmation (N7) on fresh WikiText-103 draws\n\nPublishes the frozen protocol, the sealed code and the seeds of one confirmatory study **before any of its training runs**, so the test, the decision rules and the readings are publicly fixed before any result exists.\n\n**Status at publication:**\n- **No study data exists.** No activation has been built, and no run has started.\n- The owner drew the seeds once; the source is sealed and disabled: `SOURCE_SUBJECT.json`, sha256 `7ef133ad…`.\n- The real-engine check passed on real Torch, on synthetic tokens with the real seed rows. No corpus file was read, and no study loss was computed.\n\n**What it tests:**\n- **Primary (P1, at 1e-4):** p\\*(512, E3) − p\\*(768, read at the training NLL 512 reaches at E3), six fresh draws, 95% t interval.\n- **Fixed sequence:** P1 → S1 → S3 → S4 → S5 → S2.\n- **Readings fixed in advance:** `sealed-source/PROTOCOL.md`, section 7.\n\nThe hypothesis is post hoc, from a reanalysis of N6, and N6's draws are excluded.\n\n**Limitation stated in the README:** token-level overlaps across the draws were not measured.\n\n**The owner's addendum:** `owner-decisions/OWNER_DECISIONS_ADDENDUM.md`, sha256 `c68095be0071e8aae9ead3ddce8f77f2edb765b7a4963d615c819d70150d7a4b`, named by hash because it is not bound in the seal.\n\n**Contents** (`preregistration/natural-text-matched-confirmation-20261104/`): `sealed-source/`, `seed-registry/`, `owner-decisions/`, `engine-check-result/`, `HASHES.json`, `README.md`.\n\n**Also changed:** a link in the root `README.md`, and `PUBLICATION_MANIFEST.csv` (the README row updated in place, the new files appended).\n\n**Not included:** the corpus, the real-engine check's scripts, the builder, the owner's console output and the verification script. These are named by hash in `HASHES.json`.\n\n---\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01JvfaYmnEddgunH3yg39Yo4)_","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-05T04:41:27Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T04:46:59Z","closed_at":"2026-11-05T04:44:29Z","merged_at":"2026-11-05T04:44:28Z","merge_commit_sha":"f3a2571029f4a0b4d0dc2ee974338e13996e11d8","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"rafli-hl:prereg/matched-confirmation-20261104","ref":"prereg/matched-confirmation-20261104","repo":{"id":1396932651,"node_id":"R_kgDOU0OAKw","name":"sequence-weighting-research","full_name":"rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research","owner":{"login":"rafli-hl","id":289911665,"node_id":"U_kgDOEUezcQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289911665?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl","html_url":"https://github.com/rafli-hl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Small-scale, preregistered study of sequence-weighting response (p*) across model widths: equal updates vs equal training loss. Research record.","homepage":"","language":"Python","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":["data-weighting","language-models","machine-learning","preregistration","reproducibility"],"forks_count":0,"forks":0,"stargazers_count